OOPPTTIIOONNSS
     --aa       Flush the ARC before injection.

     --bb _o_b_j_s_e_t:_o_b_j_e_c_t:_l_e_v_e_l:_s_t_a_r_t:_e_n_d
              Force an error into the pool at this bookmark tuple.  Each num‐
              ber is in hexadecimal, and only one block can be specified.

     --CC _d_v_a_s  Inject the given error only into specific DVAs.  The mask should
              be specified as a list of 0-indexed DVAs separated by commas
              (e.g. _0_,_2). This option is not applicable to logical data errors
              such as ddeeccoommpprreessss and ddeeccrryypptt.

     --dd _v_d_e_v  A vdev specified by path or GUID.

     --ee _d_e_v_i_c_e___e_r_r_o_r
              Specify
              cchheecckkssuumm    for an ECKSUM error,
              ddeeccoommpprreessss  for a data decompression error,
              ddeeccrryypptt     for a data decryption error,
              ccoorrrruupptt     to flip a bit in the data after a read,
              ddttll         for an ECHILD error,
              iioo          for an EIO error where reopening the device will
                          succeed, or
              nnxxiioo        for an ENXIO error where reopening the device will
                          fail.

              For EIO and ENXIO, the "failed" reads or writes still occur.
              The probe simply sets the error value reported by the I/O pipe‐
              line so it appears the read or write failed.  Decryption errors
              only currently work with file data.

     --ff _f_r_e_q_u_e_n_c_y
              Only inject errors a fraction of the time.  Expressed as a real
              number percentage between 00..00000011 and 110000.

     --FF       Fail faster.  Do fewer checks.

     --ff _t_x_g_s  Run for this many transaction groups before reporting failure.

     --hh       Print the usage message.

     --ll _l_e_v_e_l
              Inject an error at a particular block level.  The default is 00.

     --LL _l_a_b_e_l___e_r_r_o_r
              Set the label error region to one of nnvvlliisstt, ppaadd11, ppaadd22, or
              uubbeerr.

     --mm       Automatically remount the underlying filesystem.

     --qq       Quiet mode.  Only print the handler number added.

     --rr _r_a_n_g_e
              Inject an error over a particular logical range of an object,
              which will be translated to the appropriate blkid range accord‐
              ing to the object's properties.

     --ss _s_e_c_o_n_d_s
              Run for this many seconds before reporting failure.

     --TT _f_a_i_l_u_r_e
              Set the failure type to one of aallll, ccllaaiimm, ffrreeee, rreeaadd, or wwrriittee.

     --tt _m_o_s___t_y_p_e
